## Worksheet

**F1 – Core loop**: Game class/gameState (one state obj); mulberry32 seeds terrain/colonists/events, but `triggerAshstorm` uses `Math.random()` not `this.rng()` — not all randomness seeded. endTurn() resolves fixed steps. Score 1.

**F2 – Map**: 64-tile grid, `generateTerrain()` seeded, `isValidBuild` checks terrain, adjacency `adjBonus` (condenser/water, forge/vent) multiplies output in `produceResources`. Score 2.

**F3 – Economy**: mine→ore→forge→metal→reactor→power chains via `consume`/`produces`; caps enforced with `Math.min(…,this.caps[x])`. Score 2.

**F4 – Population**: colonists have skill/fatigue/morale/job fields, but `buildingAssignments` is never populated by any code (no assignment UI/logic) and `p.fatigue` is never read in production — skill/fatigue effectively disconnected. Score 1.

**F5 – Needs**: per-turn food/water consumption, shortage drops morale (`p.morale -= 30`), recovery (+5/turn) — but morale is never read in `produceResources`, so it never changes output. Score 1.

**F6 – Research**: 12 nodes, prereqs enforced in `research_upgrade`, costs deducted; but `renewable_power`, `biotech`, `energy_storage`, `advanced_trading` have no effect anywhere in code. Score 1.

**F7 – Events**: 10 events, 8+ with 2-3 choices with differing effects, cooldown via `eventCooldown`; but `fireRandomEvent` picks uniformly (`Math.floor(rng()*available.length)`) — not weighted. Score 1.

**F8 – Trade**: buy/sell wired (`buyTrade`/`sellTrade`), caravan qty limited; but price formula `basePrice*(0.8+rng()*0.6)*tradeMultiplier` never reads player stockpiles, and tradeMultiplier resets every caravan (no real drift). Score 1.

**F9 – Hazard**: storm severity scales with turn, reinforced_walls/storm_shelter/walls reduce damage; but buildings are simply deleted (`this.buildings[i]=null`), no partial-damage/repair state, `slowRepairTimer` set but never read anywhere. Score 1.

**F10 – Save/load**: `serialize()`/`Game.deserialize()`, save via prompt copy, load via prompt + try/catch showing `alert('Invalid save data: '+e.message)`. Score 2.

**F11 – End conditions**: win (`turn>=60 && pop>=12...`) and lose (`pop===0`) both reachable, `computeScore()` sums pop/research/turn/resources, `endGameModal` renders summary. Score 2.

**F12 – UI**: `switchTab`, log lines show `Turn ${e.turn}`, tile tooltips show terrain/adjacency bonus, keys 1-6 & Space wired, `@media(max-width:600px)` responsive CSS. Score 2.

**F13 – Dev panel**: `runTests()` has 15 real invariant checks (caps, prereqs, RNG determinism, save/load roundtrip); `runBenchmark()` runs 200 headless turns and prints a state hash. Score 2.

**G1**: `research['metallurgy']` etc. read directly in `produceResources` multiplying output; several nodes unused (energy_storage etc.) as minor gap. Score 3.

**G2**: shortage → `p.morale -= 30` is real, but morale is never read in `produceResources`, so morale never reduces labor output — chain breaks at final link. Score 1.

**G3**: `triggerAshstorm` nulls out buildings (binary destroy, not partial damage); no distinct repair cost/state — rebuilding via normal `build()` is the only "recovery", a hardcoded special case. Score 2.

**G4**: `triggerCaravan` price formula never reads `this.resources`, and `tradeMultiplier` resets every caravan visit instead of drifting. Score 0.

**G5**: `colonist_arrives` "Yes" pushes into `population` array; `ashstorm_early`/`water_contamination` choices durably subtract resources or hit morale — real, differing, persistent mutations. Score 4.

